WEBVTT

00:00:00.084 --> 00:00:03.940
SOC 2 reports are commonly discussed as Type I or Type II.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:06.522
The difference is about timing and what the auditors evaluate.

00:00:06.522 --> 00:00:10.985
A Type I report evaluates whether controls are suitably designed at a specific point in

00:00:10.985 --> 00:00:11.600
time.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.960
It answers whether the control design appears appropriate for the selected criteria and

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:16.231
scope on a defined date.

00:00:16.231 --> 00:00:20.960
A Type II report evaluates whether controls are suitably designed and operated effectively

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:22.875
over a defined review period.

00:00:22.875 --> 00:00:24.480
That period is often several months,

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.080
depending on the engagement and customer expectations.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:30.935
Type I can be useful when an organization is starting its SOC 2 journey or wants an

00:00:30.935 --> 00:00:33.040
initial independent view of control design.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.450
It can show that the organization has put a control framework in place.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:40.330
Type II usually provides stronger operational assurance because it examines whether

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.755
controls were performed over time.

00:00:42.755 --> 00:00:46.515
Customers often prefer Type II reports because they show sustained operation rather than

00:00:46.515 --> 00:00:48.125
only point-in-time design.

00:00:48.125 --> 00:00:51.480
Neither report type should be described as a badge that ends the work.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.255
Controls still need ownership, evidence, monitoring, maintenance,

00:00:54.255 --> 00:00:56.662
and improvement after the report is issued.

00:00:56.662 --> 00:00:58.575
Understanding the difference helps teams prepare.

00:00:58.575 --> 00:01:00.530
Type I emphasizes readiness on a date,

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:04.320
while Type II emphasizes consistent operation during the audit period.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.105
For teams doing the work, Type II usually requires stronger habits.

00:01:08.105 --> 00:01:10.780
Controls need to happen repeatedly, exceptions need to be tracked,

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.120
and evidence needs to show that the process was followed throughout the review window.
